Proof-angle synthesis
  Angle A: exact even-fold cover.  Prove that, outside wall rows, odd danger
    cannot cover every positive component of G.  S564 gives exact cover gaps
    for residual rows where coarse q<=14 sieves are blind.
  Angle B: wall endpoint fallback.  AP/V* have zero safe measure but retain
    closed rational witnesses; a counterexample must also kill all such
    endpoints, not merely cover G in measure.
  Angle C: recursive fine denominators.  The first witnesses for HYP-2073
    residual packets sit in the first fine window (23) or nearby fine tiers,
    matching HYP-2076's local-tier branch.
  Angle D: no-return cover chains.  A full odd cover of a G component is a
    left-to-right greedy handoff chain.  To use the user's hidden
    transitivity fact, refine odd runners into interval owner events and
    forbid return triangles in those handoffs.
